WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.326
Political theory asks two kinds

2
00:00:02.326 --> 00:00:03.508
of questions.

3
00:00:03.508 --> 00:00:04.579
What is the case,

4
00:00:04.579 --> 00:00:06.335
and what ought to be.

5
00:00:06.649 --> 00:00:08.564
Normative theory asks what ought

6
00:00:08.564 --> 00:00:09.993
to be: what is just,

7
00:00:09.993 --> 00:00:10.873
or right.

8
00:00:10.873 --> 00:00:13.220
Empirical theory studies what is,

9
00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:15.935
through observation and evidence.

10
00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:17.435
In the 1950s,

11
00:00:17.435 --> 00:00:20.384
behaviouralists like David Easton pushed

12
00:00:20.384 --> 00:00:22.657
for a science of politics.

13
00:00:22.657 --> 00:00:24.896
Easton defined politics as the

14
00:00:24.896 --> 00:00:27.929
authoritative allocation of values.

15
00:00:28.269 --> 00:00:29.215
By 1969,

16
00:00:29.215 --> 00:00:33.463
Easton himself called for post-behaviouralism.

17
00:00:33.463 --> 00:00:35.369
Research had to be relevant

18
00:00:35.369 --> 00:00:37.078
to real problems.

19
00:00:37.775 --> 00:00:39.046
Your turn.

20
00:00:39.046 --> 00:00:41.455
Whose definition is this?
